<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.10.3: The X- and Y-Intercepts of Quadratic Expressions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01907</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.10.3: The X- and Y-Intercepts of Quadratic Expressions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>55abafa1-c8ec-464f-ab9b-4109464f7f1c</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>Here are pairs of expressions in standard and factored forms. Each pair of expressions define the same quadratic function, which can be represented with the given graph.</para>
      <para>Identify the \(x\)-intercepts and the \(y\)-intercept of each graph.</para>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated">
        <item>Function \(f\)
    \(x^2+4x+3\)
    \((x+3)(x+1)\)
    
    <figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_12_06_01.svg"/></media></figure></item>
      </list>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Identify the \(x\)-intercepts of the graph.</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Graph of \(f\): \(x\)-intercepts: \((-3,0)\) and \((-1,0)\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <title>Activity</title>
        <exercise id="_67f58a73-d9ba-4806-a5a0-801efa0f1623" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            
            <para>Identify the \(y\)-value of the \(y\)-intercept of the graph.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Graph of \(f\): \(y\)-intercept \((0,3)\).</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 3. Graph of \(f\): \(y\)-intercept \((0,3)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated">
        <item>Function \(g\)
    \(x^2-5x+4\)
    \((x-4)(x-1)\)
    
    <figure><media alt="Graph of nonlinear function."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_12_06_02.svg"/></media></figure></item>
      </list>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Identify the \(x\)-intercepts of the graph.</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Graph of \(g\): \(x\)-intercepts: \((1,0)\) and \((4,0)\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="_178b12d7-ad7f-4a82-91b9-f32055d91df2" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            
            <para>Identify the \(y\)-value of the \(y\)-intercept of the graph.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Graph of \(g\): \(y\)-intercept \((0,4)\).</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 4. Graph of \(g\): \(y\)-intercept \((0,4)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated">
        <item>Function \(h\)
    \(x^2-9\)
    \((x-3)(x+3)\)
    
    <figure><media alt="Graph of nonlinear function."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_12_06_03.svg"/></media></figure></item>
      </list>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Identify the \(x\)-intercepts of the graph.</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Graph of \(h\): \(x\)-intercepts: \((3,0)\) and \((-3,0)\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="_561a8641-ac55-4e73-b668-3e53f80fb1f4" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            
            <para>Identify the \(y\)-value of the \(y\)-intercept of the graph.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!– 9, Graph of \(h\): \(y\)-intercept \((0,-9)\).</para>
            <para>The correct answer is -9. Graph of \(h\): \(y\)-intercept \((0,-9)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated">
        <item>Function \(j\)
    \(x^2-5x\)
    \( x(x-5)\)
    
    <figure><media alt="Graph of non linear function."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_12_06_04.svg"/></media></figure></item>
      </list>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Identify the \(x\)-intercepts of the graph.</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Graph of \(j\): \(x\)-intercepts: \((0,0)\) and \((5,0)\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="_3725009b-5c7a-484f-9d88-30de64a4796e" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            
            <para>Identify the \(y\)-value of the \(y\)-intercept of the graph.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 0, Graph of \(j\): \(y\)-intercept \((0,0)\).</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 0, Graph of \(j\): \(y\)-intercept \((0,0)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated">
        <item>Function \(k\)
    \(5x-x^2\)
    \(x(5-x)\)
    
    <figure><media alt="Graph of nonlinear function."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_12_06_05.svg"/></media></figure></item>
      </list>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Identify the \(x\)-intercepts of the graph.</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Graph of \(k\): \(x\)-intercepts: \((0,0)\) and \((5,0)\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="_890a1cc8-6178-4361-910f-b9f1fd5ef70d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            
            <para>Identify the \(y\)-value of the \(y\)-intercept of the graph.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 0, Graph of \(k\): \(y\)-intercept \((0,0)\).</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 0, Graph of \(k\): \(y\)-intercept \((0,0)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated">
        <item>Function \(l\)
    \(x^2+4x+4\)
    \((x+2)(x+2)\)
    
    <figure><media alt="Graph of non linear function."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_12_06_06.svg"/></media></figure></item>
      </list>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="_91e3b870-5ded-41d7-b8b2-0d67ab29631a" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            
            <para>Identify the \(x\)-intercept of the graph. 
            
            <emphasis>Answer: </emphasis> 
         </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! – 2, Graph of \(l\): \(x\)-intercept \((-2,0)\).</para>
            <para>The correct answer is – 2. Graph of \(l\): \(x\)-intercept \((-2,0)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="d8582297-86cb-47b6-9ce1-c1e401c54266" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            
            <para>Identify the \(y\)-value of the \(y\)-intercept of the graph.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Graph of \(l\): \(y\)-intercept \((0,4)\).</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 4. Graph of \(l\): \(y\)-intercept \((0,4)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <example>
        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <para>What do you notice about the \(x\)-intercepts, the \(y\)-intercept, and the numbers in the expressions defining each function? Make a couple of observations.</para>
            <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Compare your Answer:</para>
            <list>
              <item> The \(y\)-coordinate of the \(y\)-intercept is the constant term when the function is expressed in standard form. The \(y\)-intercept is \((0,-9)\) for the function \(h\), \(x^2-9\).</item>
              <item> The \(x\)-intercepts in each graph seem to match the numbers in the factors of the expressions in factored form, but the signs seem to be the opposite. For example, when the expression is \((x+3)(x+1)\), the \(x\)-intercepts are \((-3,0)\) and \((-1,0)\).</item>
              <item> When one of the factors is just a variable (rather than a sum or a difference), one of the \(x\)-intercepts is \((0,0)\). For the function \(i\), \(x(x-5)\), one of the intercepts is \((0,0)\)).</item>
              <item> x(x-5) and x(5-x) have the same \(x\)-intercepts, but one graph opens upward and the other opens downward. </item>
              <item> When the two factors are the same, there is only one \(x\)-intercept. For the function \(l\), \((x+2)(x+2)\), – 2 is the \(x\)-intercept.</item>
            </list>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </example>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated">
        <item>Here is an expression that models function \(p\), another quadratic function: \((x-9)(x-1)\).</item>
      </list>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Predict the \(x\)-intercepts of the graph that represents this function.</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>The \(x\)-intercepts will be \((9,0)\) and \((1,0)\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="c7f9f4d6-6cff-4424-897a-2c5368a6ce76" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            
            <para>Identify the \(y\)-value of the \(y\)-intercept of the graph that represents this function.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The \(y\)-intercept will be \((0,9)\) because 9 is the constant term when the expression is put in standard form.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 9. The \(y\)-intercept will be \((0,9)\) because 9 is the constant term when the expression is put in standard form.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
